{
  "_comment": [
    "Walls that already have somebody else's tag on them.",
    "",
    "Every one was stood on and read off the coordinate HUD, facing the wall. Any more you",
    "add want the same treatment -- position AND heading, because the heading is what turns",
    "Franklin square on to the paint.",
    "",
    "KEEP THEM CLOSE-ISH. The run is done on a push bike, so a wall out in El Burro is a ten",
    "minute ride each way and turns a short job into a commute. Rancho is about the limit.",
    "",
    "id       stable key; the run remembers which walls are done by it",
    "zone     GET_NAME_OF_ZONE code, for reference only",
    "gang     whose tag is on it -- decides the marker colour and who turns up",
    "x, y, z  where Franklin stands to paint",
    "heading  which way he faces, square on to the wall",
    "quiet    nobody turns out to defend this one",
    "",
    "The mission picks four at random AND skips any wall already painted -- the paint is in",
    "the save now, so a wall you have done is a wall that is yours and there is nothing left",
    "to go over. That means the pool shrinks as you work through it, and when it runs dry the",
    "run has nothing to offer until the graffiti is wiped from the reset menu."
  ],
